From: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android-gadget-start: wait for FunctionFS ep1 before binding UDC

android-gadget-start runs as ExecStartPost of android-tools-adbd.service
(Type=simple), so it races against adbd which starts writing USB
descriptors to the FunctionFS control endpoint (ep0) at the same time.

The kernel only creates ep1 (and ep2) inside /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ after adbd
has successfully written its complete descriptor set to ep0 and the FFS
state machine transitions to FFS_ACTIVE.  Binding the UDC before FFS is
in FFS_ACTIVE causes ffs_func_bind() to return -ENODEV:

    udc a600000.usb: failed to start adb: -19
    UDC core: adb: couldn't find an available UDC or it's busy

The retry loop added by the preceding patch recovers from this on the next
attempt (~1 s later), but a second problem then appears: the USB host on
the other end (the PC running adb) enumerates the device within ~100 ms
of the gadget bind, before the DWC3 ep0 state machine has finished its
post-bind initialisation.  The host's first SETUP packet hits ep0out while
it cannot accept requests:

    dwc3-qcom a600000.usb: request <ptr> was not queued to ep0out

adbd detects the broken ep0 and enters a "read descriptors / read strings"
retry loop at 1 s intervals that never recovers, because the ep0 error
leaves the DWC3 gadget in a state where subsequent bind attempts succeed
from the shell's perspective but the USB link is immediately broken again.

Fix: poll for /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ep1 before writing the UDC name.  Once ep1
exists adbd has fully written its descriptors, FFS is FFS_ACTIVE, and the
bind will succeed cleanly on the first attempt without triggering the ep0
race.  Allow up to 5 s (50 x 100 ms) and then fall through so the
existing UDC bind retry loop handles any residual edge cases.

Tested on IMDT QCS8550 SBC (dwc3-qcom, UDC a600000.usb): 20/20 boots
pass after this patch (was ~5-7/10 before).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
---
 android-gadget-start | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/android-gadget-start
+++ b/android-gadget-start
@@ -103,6 +103,22 @@ if [ -z "$best_udc" ]; then
     return 1
 fi

+# Wait for adbd to write USB descriptors to FunctionFS.  The kernel creates
+# ep1 (and ep2) inside /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ only after the descriptors have been
+# written to ep0, so ep1's existence is the reliable signal that adbd is ready
+# for the gadget to be bound to the UDC.  Binding before this causes the UDC
+# to return -ENODEV and, on a subsequent retry, an ep0out race that puts adbd
+# into a broken retry loop.
+m=0
+while [ ! -e /dev/usb-ffs/adb/ep1 ]; do
+    m=$((m + 1))
+    if [ $m -ge 50 ]; then
+        echo "Timeout waiting for adbd to write USB descriptors to FunctionFS" >&2
+        break
+    fi
+    sleep 0.1
+done
+
 echo "Binding Gadget to UDC: $best_udc (maximum_speed='$(read_max_speed "$UDC_FOLDER/$best_udc")')" >&2
 n=0
 while ! echo -n "$best_udc" > "$GADGET_PATH/UDC" 2>/dev/null; do
